# Local artifact retention

Follow `docs/development/LOCAL_ARTIFACTS.md` when creating or cleaning artifacts.
Keep private originals and inputs, live or failed work, evidence, and the current
datasets needed by active work. Historical datasets, test binaries and isolated
Wine prefixes are not permanent merely because a previous check used them.
Review dependencies and reproducibility, preview exact paths and sizes, coordinate
with active work, and retain a local receipt before retiring superseded copies.
Never use a global `target` deletion or Docker prune as unit cleanup.
For Wine prefixes never follow their links to the host. A sandbox-only process
listing or a missing lease does not establish that an old prefix is unused.
